1
00:00:00,900 --> 00:00:02,575
Paris, thirteen oh three.

2
00:00:02,525 --> 00:00:05,756
It is getting dark, and you are twelve years old.

3
00:00:05,806 --> 00:00:07,934
In front of you is a piece of silk with

4
00:00:07,884 --> 00:00:09,919
gold thread in it, half finished.

5
00:00:09,869 --> 00:00:11,626
On the table there is a candle.

6
00:00:11,576 --> 00:00:14,203
You are not allowed to light it.

7
00:00:14,253 --> 00:00:16,625
That is not your master being cheap.

8
00:00:16,575 --> 00:00:17,972
It is the law.

9
00:00:17,922 --> 00:00:21,118
This year the embroiderers of Paris wrote it into their

10
00:00:21,068 --> 00:00:24,160
rules: no work by candlelight.

11
00:00:24,203 --> 00:00:25,994
Here is the reason they give.

12
00:00:25,944 --> 00:00:29,512
Work done by candlelight comes out worse than work done

13
00:00:29,462 --> 00:00:30,186
by day.

14
00:00:30,136 --> 00:00:32,589
A candle is yellow, and it moves.

15
00:00:32,539 --> 00:00:35,643
A crooked stitch can look straight.

16
00:00:35,693 --> 00:00:37,229
So when the light goes,

17
00:00:37,179 --> 00:00:38,634
the needle goes down.

18
00:00:38,584 --> 00:00:40,967
In June, that is a long day.

19
00:00:40,917 --> 00:00:43,742
In December, it is a short one.

20
00:00:43,792 --> 00:00:46,779
You will do this for eight years.

21
00:00:46,822 --> 00:00:49,438
That is what an ordinary life is.

22
00:00:49,388 --> 00:00:50,576
Not small.

23
00:00:50,526 --> 00:00:53,943
Just made, very carefully, in daylight.
